{#
  The calendar view (FSD §8.1, kalenderkonzept.md Teil A) — three columns of
  day blocks, colour-coded by whose appointment it is.

  **Every measurement is the approved mockup's** (`mockups/preview/08-wand-kalender.png`,
  generated by `tools/mockup-gen/pages_wand.py`), taken out of that file rather
  than re-invented:

    columns   three of 805 px with a 40 px gutter, y 32 … 1408 — the 32 px
              margin is P30, not the mockup's 80 (which left 17 % of the
              panel unused for no measurable gain sideways)
    foot      legend, any failure note and the timestamp at the **bottom of the
              third column**, 36 px a line with 24 px of air above
    day title 36 px bold, 50 px line, a rule, 14 px of air  (66 px of head)
    entry     84 px, plus 38 px for every further title line
    bar       6 px [Festlegung C8] — 2 px is the proven floor, 6 px reads as a
              bar rather than a hairline; the width is configurable
    time      26 px in 185 px (28 px no longer fits beside the title), #333333
    title     32 px starting at +215 px, wrapping at ~31 characters
    location  24 px, #555555
    empty day 28 px "no appointments", 60 px  [Festlegung 2026-08-20]

  **The mockup's header is gone** [Festlegung P29, 2026-08-23]. It set the date
  at 64 px across the top with the legend beside it, and the first real image
  showed the cost: "Sunday, August 23" in the header and "Today · Sunday,
  August 23" as the first day title — the same date twice — for 140 px off
  **all three** columns. Now the date is said once, by the day title that has
  to be there anyway, and legend and timestamp sit at the foot of the third
  column. Columns one and two run the full 1.280 px.

  Two further deviations from the mockup, both measured rather than preferred:
  the rule under a day title and the gutter rule are **black**, not the
  mockup's 2 px `#aaaaaa` — a grey hairline dithers into a dotted trail on this
  panel (measured 2026-08-22, 67 % / 33 % black). Grey *text* stays grey; it is
  the thin lines that fall apart, not the areas.

  Nothing is computed in here. Wrapping, block heights and which day lands in
  which column all arrive decided from `calendar_layout.py`, for the reason the
  recipe page learned the hard way: when CSS wraps what Python budgeted, the
  column runs off the bottom of the canvas and is clipped without a word.
#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ language }}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>ePaperEngine</title>
    <style>
      html,
      body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        width: 2560px;
        height: 1440px;
        overflow: hidden;
        background: #fff;
        color: #000;
        font-family: "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif;
      }
      main {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        width: 2560px;
        height: 1440px;
        padding: 32px;
      }
      /* **No box-sizing here.** The 3 px rule sits *under* the 100 px, not
         inside it — with border-box it landed at y = 177 and pulled all three
         columns 3 px up with it (measured on the first real calendar image).
         80 + 100 + 3 + 37 = 220, the y the mockup starts the columns at. */
      /* The legend is broken into lines by calendar_layout.py, not by CSS.
         The foot is anchored to the bottom of its column, so a line more than
         the model reserved would grow *upwards* into the last appointment
         rather than being clipped where nobody notices. */
      .legend .row {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 44px;
        height: 36px;
      }
      .legend .who {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 12px;
        font-size: 28px;
        line-height: 36px;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }
      /* 34 × 24, the mockup's swatch. A filled area, so a palette colour lands
         on the panel as itself — the same reason the bars carry only the six
         Spectra primaries. */
      .legend .chip {
        width: 34px;
        height: 24px;
      }
      .stamp {
        font-size: 28px;
        line-height: 36px;
        color: #555555;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }
      /* Bottom of the third column, its height reserved in the model. */
      .foot {
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        right: 0;
        bottom: 0;
      }
      /* Only drawn when a source failed or there is nothing to show — a note
         nobody needs is 36 px of appointments. Palette red, so the line itself
         carries no dither raster. */
      .notes .line {
        font-size: 28px;
        line-height: 36px;
        color: #dc1e1e;
        white-space: nowrap;
        overflow: hidden;
      }
      .columns {
        display: flex;
        gap: 40px;
      }
      .column {
        flex: none;
        width: 805px;
        position: relative;
      }
      /* The clip is a safety net: if the height model in calendar_layout.py is
         ever off, a column stops at its own edge rather than running into the
         foot or off the canvas. Its height is set inline — the third column is
         shorter by exactly what the foot reserves. */
      .inner {
        overflow: hidden;
      }
      /* The gutter rule, in the middle of the 40 px gap. Black at 2 px for the
         measured reason above; the mockup's grey would be a dotted trail. */
      .column + .column::before {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        left: -21px;
        top: 0;
        bottom: 0;
        width: 2px;
        background: #000;
      }
      .day {
        margin: 0 0 24px 0;
      }
      .day h2 {
        margin: 0 0 14px 0;
        height: 50px;
        line-height: 50px;
        font-size: 36px;
        font-weight: bold;
        border-bottom: 2px solid #000;
        white-space: nowrap;
        overflow: hidden;
      }
      .empty {
        height: 60px;
        padding-left: 24px;
        font-size: 28px;
        line-height: 44px;
        color: #666666;
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }
      .entry {
        position: relative;
      }
      /* The colour bar carries the source [Festlegung C8]. It sits beside the
         line rather than tinting it, so it costs no line height and still
         works when a fourth calendar arrives. */
      .bar {
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        top: 0;
      }
      .time {
        position: absolute;
        left: 20px;
        top: 0;
        width: 185px;
        font-size: 26px;
        line-height: 40px;
        color: #333333;
        white-space: nowrap;
        overflow: hidden;
      }
      .what {
        position: absolute;
        left: 215px;
        top: -2px;
        width: 590px;
      }
      .what .line {
        font-size: 32px;
        line-height: 38px;
      }
      .what .where {
        font-size: 24px;
        line-height: 32px;
        color: #555555;
        white-space: nowrap;
        overflow: hidden;
        text-overflow: ellipsis;
      }
      /* Same marker as the recipe page: what did not fit is said out loud
         rather than clipped in silence [P13/P14]. */
      .cut {
        height: 46px;
        padding-top: 20px;
        font-size: 26px;
        line-height: 26px;
        color: #dc1e1e;
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>

      <div class="columns" style="height: {{ page.column_h }}px">
        {%- for column in page.columns %}
        <section class="column">
          <div class="inner" style="height: {{ page.column_h - (page.foot_h if loop.last else 0) }}px">
            {%- for day in column %}
            <div class="day">
              <h2>{{ day.title }}</h2>
              {%- if day.empty %}
              <div class="empty">{{ t("calendar.empty") }}</div>
              {%- else %}
              {%- for entry in day.entries %}
              <div class="entry" style="height: {{ entry.height }}px">
                <span
                  class="bar"
                  style="width: {{ page.bar_px }}px; height: {{ entry.height - 12 }}px; background: {{ entry.color }}"
                ></span>
                <span class="time">{{ entry.time }}</span>
                <div class="what">
                  {%- for line in entry.title_lines %}
                  <div class="line">{{ line }}</div>
                  {%- endfor %}
                  {%- if entry.location %}<div class="where">{{ entry.location }}</div>{% endif %}
                </div>
              </div>
              {%- endfor %}
              {%- if day.cut %}
              <div class="cut">{{ t("calendar.cut", count=day.cut) }}</div>
              {%- endif %}
              {%- endif %}
            </div>
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>
          {%- if loop.last and page.foot_h %}
          <div class="foot" style="height: {{ page.foot_h }}px">
            {%- if page.notes %}
            <div class="notes">
              {%- for note in page.notes %}<div class="line">{{ note }}</div>{% endfor %}
            </div>
            {%- endif %}
            <div class="legend">
              {%- for row in page.legend %}
              <div class="row">
                {%- for who in row %}
                <div class="who">
                  <span class="chip" style="background: {{ who.hex }}"></span>{{ who.label }}
                </div>
                {%- endfor %}
              </div>
              {%- endfor %}
            </div>
            <div class="stamp">{{ page.stamp }}</div>
          </div>
          {%- endif %}
        </section>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
